>## Check whether a type is a nominal type definition (record, union, wrap, or forall wrapping one). Type aliases (applications, functions, literal types, etc.) return false.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>term isNominalType = λtyp.cases(model.Type){`record`=λrt.true, `union`=λrt.true, `wrap`=λwt.true, `forall`=λfa.isNominalType (model.ForallType[body] fa), `_`=false} (strip.deannotateType typ)
#^^^^ source.hydra keyword.other.definition.hydra
#    ^ source.hydra
#     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra entity.name.function.hydra
#                  ^ source.hydra
#                   ^ source.hydra keyword.operator.equals.hydra
#                    ^ source.hydra
#                     ^ source.hydra keyword.operator.lambda.hydra
#                      ^^^ source.hydra variable.parameter.hydra
#                         ^ source.hydra punctuation.separator.binder.hydra
#                          ^^^^^ source.hydra keyword.control.hydra
#                               ^ source.hydra
#                                ^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra variable.other.qualified.hydra
#                                          ^^ source.hydra
#                                            ^ source.hydra variable.other.escaped.hydra punctuation.definition.name.begin.hydra
